Here is the `RootPort#toggleBridgeAgentFactory` function:

```solidity
function toggleBridgeAgentFactory(address _bridgeAgentFactory) external onlyOwner {
    isBridgeAgentFactory[_bridgeAgentFactory] = !isBridgeAgentFactory[_bridgeAgentFactory];

    emit BridgeAgentFactoryToggled(_bridgeAgentFactory);
}
```

The function does not perform any checks, and simply sets `isBridgeAgentFactory` for an address to the opposite of its former value.
This means that calling `toggleBridgeAgent` on an EOA account for example, sets `isBridgeAgentFactory` for that account to !false because the default boolean value in mappings is false.
So now, `isBridgeAgentFactory` for that EOA account has been set to true, so EOA can directly call `addBridgeAgent` function.
