# Vulnerability details

`BranchBridgeAgent._normalizeDecimals()` and `BranchPort._denormalizeDecimals()` are incorrect as they are implemented in a reversed manner, such that `_denormalizeDecimals()` is normalizing to 18 decimals while `_normalizeDecimals()` is denormalizing to the underlying token decimals.

The result is that for tokens with > 18 decimals, `_normalizeDecimals()` will overscale the decimals, while for tokens with < 18 decimals, `_normalizeDecimals()` will underscale the decimals.

## Impact
As `_normalizeDecimals()` and `_denormalizeDecimals()` are used to derive the amount of hToken for the bridging of deposit, it will cause an incorrect accounting of hTokens and underlying tokens in the system. 


