# Vulnerability details

## Impact
getRebalance at TalosManager would suffer underflows when currentTick becomes smaller than the tickLower() of the position, leading to failure to performUpkeep.


getRebalance is done by comparing the currentTick with the position's range, if the lower or upper tick is more different from the current tick beyond a certain rebalance threshold, it would return `true`. However if the currentTick becomes smaller than the `tickLower()` of the position, the first comparison would trigger function revert due to underflow.

```solidity
    function getRebalance(ITalosBaseStrategy position) private view returns (bool) {
        //Calculate base ticks.
        (, int24 currentTick,,,,,) = position.pool().slot0();

@underflow possible        return currentTick - position.tickLower() >= ticksFromLowerRebalance
            || position.tickUpper() - currentTick >= ticksFromUpperRebalance;
    }
```
