The rugpull bug allows the contract owner to manipulate the conversion rate, giving them an unfair advantage in claiming rewards. 
By setting a higher conversion rate, the owner can inflate their claimable rewards compared to other users. This creates an imbalance in the reward distribution, favoring the owner and potentially causing financial harm to other participants 
By setting a lower conversion rate, the owner  can reduce the claimable amounts for rewards for users and effectively performing a rugpull. This manipulation limits the rewards that users can rightfully claim.

