## Impact

Using `tx.gasPrice` to calculate the gas cost is not credible, because `tx.gasPrice` can be manipulated at will. By setting `tx.gasPrice` to minimum, the gas cost is minimum, which leads to the protocol being unable to pay out.  

## Proof of Concept

When a user interacts with `BranchBridgeAgent`, maia checks `requiresFallbackGas`, and when it passes, maia calls `anyCall` 
to forward cross-chain messages, which integrates multichain and relies on the middleware `AnycallExecutor`. When the message is executed on `RootBridgeAgent`, the gas cost is calculated through `tx.gasPrice`.  
The problem is that `tx.gasPrice` is controllable. Through private miner pools such as flashbot or bloXroute, `tx.gasPrice` can be set to the lowest: baseFee(EIP-1559) on Ethereum, 0 on BSC. 
