# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Detailed description of the impact of this finding.
The function updatePeriod() from the base minter contract,which functions as a means to share weekly emissions between gauges and DAO, the intended functionality for the method according to the docs clearly states that the function should be called after every 7 days(which is a guage cycle), the issue is noticed after a call is made to the function and the method it uses to update the variable activePeriod(which represents the last time the function is called).ActivePeriod is updated as a function of (block.timestamp/weekly)*weekly which in regular maths it should be same as block.timestamp, but this isn't so because solidity as a class based language doesn't support decimals .lets take for example that the current block.timestamp=1687605817 and the gauge cycle is over then activePeriod is(1687605817/604800)=2.790353533×10³ since solidity rounds decimal point to zero we will get 2790,
activePeriod =2790×604800=1.687392×10⁹.if we do the calculation between the difference between the current block.timestamp and active period we would get 213817(almost 2.5 days) which means that from the last call to updatePeriod we could also make a call to the updatePeriod() after 4.5 days this causes discrepancies and the difference compounds again after calling the function over and over .
